From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abue Ammar <14371506+abue-ammar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:05:56 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Show animations toggle to General settings (#1692)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Show animations toggle in General › Appearance, on by default. Off,
every Tinycast surface opens, closes and changes at once: SwiftUI
transitions, the palette and panel window animations, HUD and preview
fades, and the Notes move. On, nothing changes, and Reduce Motion still
trims movement where it did. Activity indicators keep running.

AppCore projects the setting into Motion.isEnabled. Every hosting root
applies motionScope(), which strips the animation from each transaction
beneath it, so no animation site checks the setting itself. Panels that
open with the document-window animation adopt AnimatedPanel, and
AppKit animation groups take their duration from Motion.duration(_:).
